  "rationale": "Direct-match hypertension candidates are present (e.g., PGS000706, PGS001320, PGS001838, PGS002047, PGS002296, PGS002335/2407/2456/2505/2554/2603/2652/2701, PGS002765, PGS002777/2778, PGS002994–PGS003028, PGS004191–PGS004194, PGS004234/4236, PGS004455/4525/4526, PGS004785–PGS004788, PGS004934, PGS005144/5153). Among models with PRS-comparable metrics, PGS001320 (Hypertension; snpnet) provides explicit PGS-only AUROC=0.629 and PGS-only R2=0.06493, plus incremental AUROC=0.04424, with basic covariates (age, sex, UKB array type, PCs) and a large UKB-based development/validation (n=67,425), making it the most directly supported by visible standalone-PRS performance evidence. However, domain_knowledge flags pan-trait framework-derived sparse/snpnet models (the '813 traits' paper family that includes PGS001320) as often underperforming disease-focused alternatives in external validation; several other hypertension candidates come from different study archetypes (e.g., multi-ethnic hypertension PRS papers PGS004234/PGS004236, or other disease-focused studies) but lack PRS-only metrics in this context, preventing a clearly high-confidence best choice. This unresolved study-archetype vs. metric-availability tension keeps the selection sub-optimal."
